# Wave T44 (Honeyfield kit): bloomroof — Honeyfield's own roof, worn by the shipped House's th cells and both facade cottages. BLOOM-PETAL SHINGLE: magenta-pink petal scales in overlapping courses with petal-tip highlights and cream blossom flecks — 'every roof a garden that got promoted' (the town's own dialogue). Overlapping organic SCALES: unlike Blossom's sakuraroof (pale slabs), Hushmoor's shingleroof (dark violet shingle) and Wildflower's trellisroof (open lattice). (NO-SAME-KIT law; WAVE-T44-HONEYFIELD-PLAN.md §5.)
